From 204d22b8b7766ac67633728d9769c30d49be651b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anyingiit <winshyon@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 17:20:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(graphics): stop EncodeSixel allocating per pixel

buildPalette read every pixel through image.Image.At and
color.RGBAModel.Convert, and the band loop did the same again before
quantising each pixel with color.Palette.Convert: every read boxed a
color.Color. Colour switches and runs were then formatted with
fmt.Sprintf. BenchmarkEncodeSixel made ~51,000 allocations per frame.

Pixels are now read with rgbaAt, as EncodeKitty's resize already does.
buildPalette returns []color.RGBA plus each colour's index, and
paletteIndex looks an exact 8-bit match up in that map and otherwise
runs color.Palette.Index's nearest-colour search on the unboxed values,
so the chosen index is the same for every image type. Numbers are
appended with strconv.AppendInt.

BenchmarkEncodeSixel: 51,211 allocs/op, 371 KB/op -> 11 allocs/op,
166 KB/op. The escape sequence is unchanged byte for byte (checked on
RGBA, NRGBA, RGBA64, Gray and >256-colour images, opaque and
transparent). TestEncodeSixelDoesNotAllocatePerPixel keeps a 480x384
frame under 100 allocations (it makes 41).

Closes #59
---
